Q. What is AWS CodeDeploy (Automated Deployments)?
A:	AWS CodeDeploy is a fully managed deployment service that automates application deployments to
EC2 instances
ECS (Amazon Elastic Container Service)
AWS Lambda functions
On-premises servers
Feature
Description
Automated Deployments
No manual intervention needed
Deployment Strategies
Supports in-place, blue/green, canary, linear deployments
Rollback Support
Automatically reverts if deployment fails
Lifecycle Hooks
Run scripts at each deployment phase
Monitoring
Integrates with CloudWatch, CloudTrail, and SNS
Security
IAM-controlled access, logs in CloudWatch


Q. What is AWS CodePipeline (CI/CD Workflow)?
A:	AWS CodePipeline is a fully managed CI/CD workflow service that automates the build, test, and deployment stages of application delivery.
Feature
Description
End-to-End CI/CD
Automates code flow from commit to deploy
Custom Stages
Source → Build → Test → Deploy (flexible pipeline stages)
Integrations
Native support for GitHub, CodeBuild, CodeDeploy, S3, Lambda
Visual Pipeline Editor
Easy drag-and-drop UI or JSON/YAML definitions
Event-driven
Automatically triggers on code changes
Approval Gates
Manual approvals between stages possible


CodeCommit → stores the code
CodeBuild → compiles/tests it 
CodeDeploy → automates deployment
CodePipeline → orchestrates the workflow end-to-end
